      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start/tone, but i think the marketing department is going to push back. \n\nthe score of 5 is a bit low for our current campaign standards. they really want to see these emails hitting a much higher \"richness\" score to justify the automation. \n\ncan you try another version? keep the same warm/professional vibe, but try to weave in more of those features from the list so the score is higher. just... be careful not to make it look like a list. keep it feeling natural and helpful so it doesn't get flagged as spam.",
